{"step_index":1167,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:32:55Z","thinking":"**Reviewing Proxy Ignore List**\n\nThe current proxy configuration uses manual mode with a defined list of ignored hosts. The list of ignored hosts does not include the target domain `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`. This absence of the domain from the ignore list implies the proxy should handle requests to that domain.\n\n\n**Hypothesizing Brave Proxy Bypass**\n\nBrave's Chromium network stack uses GNOME's proxy settings; requests not in the `ignore-hosts` list are routed through the proxy. The target domain `*.outremer-telecom.fr` is not in the ignore list, thus it uses the proxy, which then causes a timeout. Adding `'*.outremer-telecom.fr'` to `ignore-hosts` would bypass the proxy and use the local `/etc/hosts` resolution, likely resolving the timeout.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"curl -x http://a.samy:koby_%40miT_S%40My@172.16.75.9:3128 -i https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing Squid proxy behavior on port 9443\"","toolSummary":"\"Curl through Squid proxy\""}}]}
