{"step_index":1174,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:33:20Z","thinking":"**Investigating Proxy-Hosts Resolution Behavior**\n\nThe observed behavior suggests that when a corporate forward proxy is enabled and a domain is *not* excluded, browsers bypass `/etc/hosts` resolution and directly attempt connection through the proxy. This implies that the proxy is taking precedence for all non-excluded domains, preventing local DNS resolution.\n\nThis could explain the connection issues, since it could be assuming that the proxy is configured to resolve this particular domain. We need to determine if `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` is meant to be proxied or resolved locally.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"gsettings set org.gnome.system.proxy ignore-hosts \\\"['dev.intranet.local', 'localhost', '127.0.0.0/8', '::1', 'omt.local', '.omt.local', 'intranet.local', '.intranet.local', '172.30.0.0/16', '172.16.0.0/16', '10.1.0.0/16', '172.17.0.0/16', '10.2.41.0/24', '10.1.41.0/24', '172.17.12.0/24', '10.3.41.0/24', '10.6.41.0/24', 'grok.com', '*.grok.com', 'x.ai', '*.x.ai', 'outremer-telecom.fr', '*.outremer-telecom.fr']\\\" && gsettings get org.gnome.system.proxy ignore-hosts\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Adding outremer-telecom.fr to GNOME proxy ignore list\"","toolSummary":"\"Update GNOME proxy ignore-hosts\""}}]}
