{"step_index":1183,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:33:53Z","thinking":"**Identifying the Proxy Bypass**\n\nThe service status reports as \"UP\". Examining the desktop configuration reveals that `/etc/hosts` correctly resolves a specific domain. However, an HTTP forward proxy is present, which, if used, would bypass the local host file resolution. The proxy, in this case, would direct traffic away from the `/etc/hosts` entry. This explains the observed issue.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"sudo -n true 2>&1 || echo \\\"Requires password\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing sudo on local machine\"","toolSummary":"\"Check local sudo\""}}]}
