{"step_index":1215,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:38:18Z","content":"Done! The changes are applied and verified end-to-end.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Verification of `/etc/environment`\n\nBoth `no_proxy` and `NO_PROXY` now cleanly bypass `outremer-telecom.fr`:\n```text\nhttp_proxy=\"http://a.samy:koby_%40miT_S%40My@172.16.75.9:3128\"\nhttps_proxy=\"http://a.samy:koby_%40miT_S%40My@172.16.75.9:3128\"\nHTTP_PROXY=\"http://a.samy:koby_%40miT_S%40My@172.16.75.9:3128\"\nHTTPS_PROXY=\"http://a.samy:koby_%40miT_S%40My@172.16.75.9:3128\"\nno_proxy=\".intranet.local,localhost,127.0.0.0/8,::1,outremer-telecom.fr,.outremer-telecom.fr\"\nNO_PROXY=\".intranet.local,localhost,127.0.0.0/8,::1,outremer-telecom.fr,.outremer-telecom.fr\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Proof that `apt update` still works 100%\n\nWe ran a live `sudo apt-get update`:\n```text\nConnecting to HTTP proxy (http://172.16.75.9:3128)\nHit:1 https://security.debian.org/debian-security trixie-security InRelease\nHit:2 https://deb.debian.org/debian trixie InRelease\nHit:3 https://deb.nodesource.com/node_20.x nodistro InRelease\nGet:4 https://deb.debian.org/debian trixie-updates InRelease [47.3 kB]\nFetched 5,941 kB in 7s (904 kB/s)\nReading package lists... Done\n```\nAll Debian repositories continue to route through your Squid proxy as normal.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Proof that Centreon Map connects with 200 OK\n\nExecuting a native curl with the new environment:\n```text\n< HTTP/2 200 \n< server: nginx\n< access-control-allow-origin: *\n< access-control-allow-methods: GET, POST, OPTIONS, PUT, DELETE\n< content-type: application/vnd.spring-boot.actuator.v3+json\n\n{\"status\":\"UP\"}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Now test in your Centreon Web UI!\n\n1. Open your browser on Centreon: **Administration > Extensions > Options**.\n2. Click **\"Test connection to server\"** on `MAP Engine server address`.\n3. It will turn **<span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">Green</span>**!"}
